# ★ PINNED, NOT ASSESSED.
#
# Published 2026-09-29, eight days after the other three were pinned and on the
# day this project's week-13 summary was being written. It is pinned the same
# day so that the weekly job watches it for drift like the others, and so that
# "three advisories" stops being a sentence about all of them.
#
# What is NOT here, on purpose: a verdict. The other three were each decided
# five ways (harness/run_exposure.sh) and the verdicts are asserted by
# check_advisories.py --check against docs/advisories.md. This one has had two
# of those five, read by hand on the day:
#
#   ANCESTRY  the fix for 4.0 is PR #3902, merged 2026-09-22 as 7e7909d. The
#             `pqc` flavor pins libspdm 8a92317, the 4.0.0-rc tag of
#             2026-08-04, which is older than the fix; `stable` pins 3.8.0,
#             and the fix for that line arrived in 3.8.3. Neither pinned tree
#             carries it.
#   CHAIN     this project's own chain (certs/out/) has CA:TRUE on the root and
#             the intermediate and NO pathLenConstraint and NO nameConstraints
#             on either — precondition 1 does not hold for any capture made with
#             it. DMTF's sample chains, which the matrix arms use, are a
#             separate question and were not read.
#
# Two observations are not a verdict, and a document that printed one from them
# would be doing exactly what standing rule 21 is about. The assessment is
# week 14's first task.
#
# THE ADVISORY'S OWN LIMIT, worth repeating wherever it is cited: the mbedtls
# back end is not fully mitigated even in the patched releases, because mbedtls
# does not enforce nameConstraints (Mbed-TLS/mbedtls#8759). This project links
# the OpenSSL back end.
#
# NOT IN GITHUB'S GLOBAL ADVISORY DATABASE; https://github.com/advisories/
# GHSA-7vfm-9mfh-j8p5 returned 404 on 2026-09-29. url= above is the one that
# resolves. Not vendored, for third_party/dmtf-2026-0002.pin's reason.
